  "ingredients": [
    "4 tart green apples",
    "0.5 cup brown sugar",
    "2 teaspoons ground cinnamon",
    "¼ teaspoon kosher salt",
    "4 tablespoons butter"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients, and preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/pKtonZ_4lM5bHh9J3i2mnZ6t0AQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21127-baked-apples-ddmfs-step1-4x3-0274-0be86c2c4a264cf9ad3f1fcb8164f802.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21127/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using an apple corer, a melon baller, or a teaspoon, remove core from the top of each apple, making sure not to go all the way to the bottom, leaving about 1 ½ inches from the bottom of the apple.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/HeVhQMoAH4lyMCowz304brHZ6eU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21127-baked-apples-ddmfs-step2-4x3-0274-50686381c3f84b59846275e375902041.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21127/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir sugar, cinnamon, and salt together in a small bowl until evenly combined. Stuff each apple with 2 tablespoons brown sugar mixture.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/8N8S-_xZI2O3PiOZ-QUlYd8XmlY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21127-baked-apples-ddmfs-step3-4x3-0275-c5efb37e2e404683bdf003a20ccb8ace.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21127/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place apples in an 8-inch square baking dish. Top each apple with 1 piece of butter; pour boiling water to a depth of 1/4-inch in the bottom of the dish. Cover with foil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/1M5TyITRj3j1M1K98C2RY6EClnI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21127-baked-apples-ddmfs-step4-4x3-0277-411dd9423a3b427b97f2f2d2485af7cc.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21127/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 20 minutes. Remove foil and continue to bake, uncovered, until sugar begins to caramelize and apples are tender when pierced with a paring knife, 20 to 25 minutes more.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/sGn_OEgUztCLSU1Xi8US6WfvXD8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21127-baked-apples-ddmfs-step5-4x3-0277-92f266dce73a46bb92efd01f1fdde67c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21127/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve warm. Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/vGq7vLrtORK_BIXaMpZKJ3F4U5M=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21127-baked-apples-ddmfs-beauty-4x3-0277-1-ef64537a97d64dc295a07ac5f7866bb1.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21127/step_06.webp"
    }
  ],
